cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "xMC_Extinction: R(V)-dependent analytic extinction curves for SMC, LMC and LMC2 dust"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sandhya
    family-names: Sanil Kumar
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6557-3044"
    affiliation: "Indian Institute of Space Science and Technology, Thiruvananthapuram"
  - given-names: Vikram
    family-names: Khaire
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8433-5099"
    affiliation: "Indian Institute of Technology, Tirupati"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sandhyasanil/xMC_Extinction"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-30"       
abstract: "This package contains code to compute V-band normalised extinction for LMC, LMC2 (LMC Supershell), and SMC dust for a given R(V). The models are developed using the Cardelli et al. (1989) framework and data from Gordon et al. (2003) for the LMC and LMC2 and Gordon et al. (2024) for the SMC. Each model takes two inputs: wavenumber (x=1/λ) in units of inverse microns and R(V), and returns the corresponding A(λ)/A(V). The model is valid for x values ranging from 0.455 to 8 μm⁻¹ (2.2 μm to 1250 Å) and R(V) values from 2 to 5.6 for the SMC, 3.15 to 3.96 for the LMC and 1.68 to 3.41 for the LMC2."
keywords:
  - interstellar dust
  - extinction curves
  - Magellanic Clouds
